								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;"><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=3011.msg34566#msg34566">Quote from: Look everyone! I can stick my foot in my Mouth(matician) on August 02, 2007, 02:59:30 pm</a></div><div class="quote">Does this include people/artist who speak out against the war, and sell CD&#039;s?<br /><br />Isn&#039;t that an ammedment violation?<br /></div><br />yes<br /><br />and yes<br /><br />of course tony snow says it won&#039;t be used that way  <img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Smileys/default/rolleyes.gif" alt="Roll Eyes" border="0" /> , and we just need to trust them... but several lawyers have said that its writen so broadly, and defines so few of its terms that it could very well be used to target protesters, people who donate to charities that might assist possible insurgents, possibly even media outlets that have been determined to hurt the war effort.  these would all be extreme interpretations, but the interpretations aren&#039;t made by a jury, or even  judge, they&#039;ll be made by bush administration appointees in the treasury department, or other government officials appointed by them.  so who&#039;s to say they can&#039;t make extreme interpretations.  and if thats not fucked up enough, they don&#039;t even have to tell you that they&#039;re gonna take your stuff, they don&#039;t even have to tell you after they&#039;ve taken it.  you could just be livin life and all of a sudden you&#039;re bank accounts credit cards ... wouldn&#039;t work anymore and the re-po guys come and start hallin all your shit away, and they don&#039;t even have to tell you they are doing it, let alone why or what evidence they&#039;re basing it on.  this is insanly unconstitutional and i have barely heard a peep out of most mainstream news outlets about it.  and i haven&#039;t heard that congress has even mentioned it.<br /><br />i used to think people who said this kind of thing were a bit crazy, but now i think the people who wonder if we&#039;re going to have an election in &#039;08, and if we do, if bush is gonna leave office in &#039;09 are just pessimistic, i hate to say it, but i concider a coup a slight but real possibility at this point.  the preparations have all basically been made.</div>
